More hints:  (semi-spoilers)


Stay unburdened.  Don't try to carry really heavy corpses around -- you're
toast if attacked by a strong monster while strained or overtaxed, and
the time it takes to carry it to an altar will probably mean that your
sacrifice will be rejected anyway.  Better to kill heavy stuff on the
altar.

Be careful until you gain intrinsic speed.  For Valkyries and Barbarians,
this comes at level 7.  Once you have it, you can run away unless you're
surrounded.  You can also smack stuff twice as often.

If about to die, pray.

Keep a few missile weapons or at least rocks/daggers handy for throwing
at monsters.  Never attack a floating eye or jelly hand-to-hand unless
you know you are immune to the return attack.

Dwarven mithril coats are really nice.

Don't mess with fountains unless you either just started and don't care
about the character, or you are powerful enough to handle anything
nasty that might happen.

Ditto with sinks.

Don't let your pet die if you can help it.  It might save your butt,
or let you rob a shop the safe way.

Don't mess with shopkeepers.  Pay, or let your pet steal.  

Don't get surrounded.  Fight in corridors, with a stairway behind you,
if at all possible.

Watch the status line.

Keep trying.

